.TH HMW-RELAYCTL 8 "" "helpbuoy" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hmw-relayctl \- run hmw-relay admin commands on the system relay
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hmw-relayctl
.I command
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hmw-relayctl
runs
.BR hmw-relay (1)
as the hmw-relay system user on the state of the hmw-relay service in
.IR /var/lib/hmw-relay ,
so the files it writes stay readable by the service. It must be run as root.
The running relay picks up changes within a second.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
sudo hmw-relayctl hostkey
sudo hmw-relayctl helper add alice 'ssh\-ed25519 AAAA...'
sudo hmw-relayctl helper list
sudo hmw-relayctl client list
sudo hmw-relayctl client remove SHA256:...
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/hmw-relay
Listen address of the service.
.TP
.I /var/lib/hmw-relay
Host key, helpers, registered clients and relay.log.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR hmw-relay (1)
